{
  "key": "tusker-retreat",
  "name": "Tusker Retreat",
  "kind": "dungeon",
  "sources": {
    "landblocks": "the dats: landblock 0x5C49 (GroundDraft)",
    "arrival": "the pinned world SQL v0.9.296: weenie 22694's Destination (PositionType 2) is the arrival cell 0x5C490138 at (89.8429, -116.371, 0.005) (GroundDraft; a read-only SELECT on weenie_properties_position object_Id 22694 position_Type 2 agrees)",
    "walk": "the doorway lean 0.3, the island re-draft's (M6 4 R1) and the Burrow's: GroundDraft from the arrival 0x5C490138 reaches 169 of the landblock's 180 floored cells at lean 0, 0.3, 0.6 and 0.9 alike (72 of the 252 cells floorless); the 11 floored cells it does not reach are pockets: 0x5C49010B, 0x010F and 0x0113 (z 0, each joined only to a floorless cell over the z -6 rooms) and 0x0182, 0x0183, 0x0187, 0x018A, 0x018B, 0x018E, 0x018F and 0x0190 (z 6, a ring round the floorless cells 0x0188, 0x0189, 0x018C and 0x018D, the open shaft over the z 0 room 0x0126): every portal out of them fits the body but is neither a doorway, a floor crossing nor a stair (RoomGraph.IsPassable false), so 11 of the 71 slots stand where no walk goes: the profile hunts the slots its walk reaches (RespawnSchedule: a target slot in a walkable cell), TODO(m6-retreat-pockets) (see targets and hunt). The leg's stop rules are the Burrow's (stop within 1.0 m, dwell 0.25 s, a leg at most 90 s), not measured on this ground",
    "storeys": "the dats (GroundDraft.Cells): every cell the arrival 0x5C490138 reaches over the doorways RoomGraph.IsPassable accepts at lean 0.3, grouped by origin z; 169 walkable cells in 4 storeys (z 12: 75, z 6: 48, z 0: 37, z -6: 9) of 252; 72 floorless and 11 unreached pocket cells left out",
    "no_go": "the pinned world SQL v0.9.296: the exit portal's cell (a portal whose Destination is outside 0x5C49): 0x5C490100 (wcid 22695 'Surface' to 0xF97E0035); it holds two Tusker Kin slots (22510 and 22509, guids 0x75C49001 and 0x75C49002), so 69 slots stand outside it; no other cell is held back here (the hunt's keep-out is in hunt)",
    "targets": "the pinned world SQL v0.9.296 through GroundDraft.World: the four weenies of the generator's 71 slots with Name and Level: Male Tusker 11 (level 20, 30 slots), Female Tusker 236 (15, 11), Tusker Kin 22509 (15, 7) and Tusker Kin 22510 (20, 23); none carries a tusk (no create-list row of 22423 or 22427 on these four weenies: the Female Tusk errand stays on tusker-burrow). Roles: all targets; 22510 kill-first: it casts (weenie_properties_spell_book: Flame, Frost, Acid Stream, Shock Wave, Lightning, Force and Whirling Blade I, Imperil Other I and Bludgeoning Vulnerability Other I) and the simulator puts its harm at 0.64 health a second against a Male Tusker's 0.60 for 1.14 casts of Flame Bolt III a kill against 2.12 (pwsh -File tools\\fight-sim.ps1 matchup 22510 --her Winnie and matchup 11 --her Winnie, 2026-11-19, Winnie at level 8), so a cast on it takes twice the harm off her a cast on a Male does; the level-15 Kin 22509 hits for 0 (its two body parts DVal 2; matchup 22509: 0.00 health a second over 4,777 attacks). The Kin are CreatureType 31 (Human) with FriendType 8 (Tusker), the tuskers CreatureType 8 with no FriendType (weenie_properties_int types 2 and 72): a woken Kin alerts the tuskers near it, a woken tusker no Kin (Monster_Awareness.cs AlertFriendly @95ef426d). Stats: max_health and magic_defence from the bestiary (from_bestiary, the same pinned rows: GroundCreatureNumbersTests); attributes and damage_types as GroundDraft drafted them (weenie_properties_attribute types 1 to 6, the OR of weenie_properties_body_part d_Type); swing_s not drafted (TODO(f11-swing-seconds))",
    "level_band": "the pinned world SQL v0.9.296 through GroundDraft.World, the draft's rule (the targets' levels only, GroundDraft.LevelBandOf): the targets are level 15 to 20; the climber's band is the ladder rung's 10-14 (ladder/war-mage.json, rung burrow), and a dungeon's pick is not banded by the rung's margin (TODO(m6-dungeon-band))",
    "portal": "none: the entry portal, weenie 22694 Tusker Retreat (guid 0x7F97E000), has PortalBitmask 0x31 (PropertyInt 111; a read-only SELECT reads 49), which carries NoRecall (0x20, ACE.Entity/Enum/PortalBitmask.cs:15 @95ef426d), and ACE's Portal.NoTie is NoRecall (Portal_Properties.cs:14-16), so it cannot be tied and the ground has no tie record (the entry section holds its place)",
    "home": "Holtburg's lifestone in cell 0xA9B40019 and the known point (84, 7.7) off it, z 94, the Burrow's and the Lodge's home (tusker-burrow.json sources.home; D48: the island has no lifestone and the tusker portals are NoRecall); the draft's town half named the same lifestone, guid 0x7A9B404F at (81.3304, 11.7974, 94.005), 18,545 m from the portal; the point is the climber's standing point (TODO(m6-ground-live-facts))",
    "vendors": "the Burrow's rows verbatim (tusker-burrow.json sources.vendors has each row's source and price rule): the 10-14 rung's Holtburg shops, the same climber at the same levels; Oolutanga's Refuge's Mage 22721 and Healer 22725 are not vendors here (TODO(m6-island-vendors), D48)",
    "spell_plan": "the Burrow's rows verbatim (tusker-burrow.json sources.spell_plan): Flame Bolt II for 10-15 (the projected base War Magic 110 at level 10 and 133 at 14, II at 0.95; III needs 143: SpellPlan.LevelAt, ladder rung burrow sources.spell_level) and III for 16-21; the fight casts by the live cap on her buffed War Magic (D129), which these rows do not lower",
    "components": "the Burrow's lines verbatim (tusker-burrow.json sources.components): the foci formula of Flame Bolt II and III and the account test's formula beside it",
    "supplies": "the Burrow's stock, kit, burden line and purse verbatim (tusker-burrow.json sources.supplies has each line's sizing): the same rung (10-14), spells and shops. The lines were sized on the Burrow's kill rate; the Retreat's is not measured (the simulator's casting-only ceiling, 2.21 M XP an hour, pwsh -File tools\\fight-sim.ps1 rank --her Winnie --min-level 5 --max-level 40, cache/fight-sim/rank-Winnie-5-40.grounds.tsv, is no rate): TODO(m6-retreat-live) reads the burn on the first fresh climb",
    "hold_spots": "none: the loop walks the tour and holds no spot",
    "respawn": "the pinned world SQL v0.9.296: the one generator instance of the landblock, guid 0x75C49013 (wcid 7932, the Lodge's generator weenie) in 0x5C490137, its delay 240 s from its first profile row (weenie_properties_generator) and its tick 60 s from RegenerationInterval (PropertyFloat 41); its 71 slots are its landblock_instance_link children (cell, wcid)",
    "tour": "a first draft (GroundDraft.FirstTour), as the Burrow's: the cells of the target slots in walkable cells but the exit's, storey by storey from the highest z down, nearest first by cell origin from the arrival",
    "outdoor": "none: a dungeon"
  },
